  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proposal Development for DACHEP/PASADA - Comic Relief Application</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collaboration between DACHEP and PASADA began before Comic Relief funding.  CAFOD has been in a funding relationship with Comic Relief over the past 3 years. CR funded DACHEP/PASADA through CAFOD on strengthening Community Responses to HIV and AIDS in Dar and the Coastal areas in Tanzania. The funding which commenced in October 2004 ended in September 2007.

The Implementation of the DP community based project was a success; it has had impressive results and has potential to grow further and achieve more impact.  It is an example of successful collaboration between two independent entities to create greater impact in response to HIV and AIDS.

Based on the successful implementation, and the good relationship established with CR from this project, CR has indicated that a second phase would be a good chance for additional funding. 
This is therefore an opportunity to seek additional funding for this program from Comic Relief.  CAFOD and partners makes a new proposal for the project grant in January 2008. Consequently a mini workshop was held at Gracia Garden, Nairobi on 8th November for the purpose of developing a draft summary application.</narrative>
  </description>
